      "description": "Source descriptors (`folio-source-descriptor/v1`): how to ENUMERATE WHO IRIS and ask it for a SUBSET, so an agent asked for part of it is not told the API by a human every time. Moved here from large-datasets' `sources/` on 2026-10-01 (owner ruling: large-datasets dissolves into cat-harness; bean `j7ql`), because a descriptor is ABOUT one corpus and the instance that holds or catalogues that corpus owns it — the schema stays in cat-harness. Its far-apart sibling, Lean mathlib, is in folio-assistant-sci: IRIS items stand alone (`subsetIsSelfContained: true`), three identifier systems, paged REST.",
